.TH DWMBLOCKSR 1 dwmblocksr\-VERSION
.SH NAME
dwmblocksr \- modular status bar for dwm (Rust port of dwmblocks)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dwmblocksr
.RB [ \-d
.IR delim ]
.RB [ \-p ]
.RB [ \-v ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
dwmblocksr builds dwm's status text from blocks, each the first line of the
output of a shell command, and sets it as the name of the root window, which
dwm draws in its bar. It is a port of dwmblocks to Rust with the same
behaviour.
.P
Every block has an icon, a command, an update interval in seconds and an
update signal. A block's command runs with
.B /bin/sh \-c
every
.I interval
seconds (never if 0) and whenever dwmblocksr receives the signal
SIGRTMIN+\fIsignal\fR, e.g.
.BR "pkill \-RTMIN+10 dwmblocksr" .
The blocks are put together in order, separated by the delimiter; a block
whose icon and output are both empty is left out. A block's text is cut to
100 bytes, never in the middle of a UTF\-8 character.
.P
By default the commands run in parallel, so a slow command does not hold up
the other blocks, and a command that is still running when its block is due
again is left to finish and run again afterwards.
.P
Status2d colour codes such as ^2^ or ^c#rrggbb^, in icons or in command
output, are passed to dwm unchanged.
.SH CLICKABLE BLOCKS
Each block with a signal starts with that signal as a byte (1 to 31), which
dwm's statuscmd patch uses to find the clicked block. dwm then sends the
block's signal with
.BR sigqueue (3),
the mouse button as the value. dwmblocksr runs the block's command in the
background with
.B BLOCK_BUTTON
set to the button and its output discarded, and updates the block
afterwards. A signal sent with
.BR kill (1)
only updates the block.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-d " delim"
use
.I delim
instead of the configured delimiter (at most
.B delimlen
bytes of it).
.TP
.B \-p
write the status to standard output, one line whenever it changes, instead
of setting the root window name; blocks then have no signal byte.
.TP
.B \-v
prints version information to stderr, then exits.
.SH CONFIGURATION
dwmblocksr reads
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/dwmblocksr/config.toml
(normally
.IR ~/.config/dwmblocksr/config.toml )
at startup; every key is optional and defaults to the built\-in
configuration. A file that fails to parse is reported on stderr and ignored.
The keys are
.B blocks
(a list of
.BR "{ icon, command, interval, signal }" ),
.B delim
(the delimiter, default " "),
.B delimlen
(the most bytes of it used, default 5) and
.B async
(false runs the commands one at a time, default true).
Changes take effect when dwmblocksr is restarted.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGTERM, SIGINT
exit, after clearing the root window name so dwm shows its default text.
.TP
.B SIGRTMIN+n
update every block with signal
.IR n ;
with a sigqueue value, click them.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dwm (1),
.BR dwmr (1)
